        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Shared Method 1 (preferred, aerobic): Cu(OAc)2·4H2O (0.59 g, 3.0 mmol), Ln(OAc)3·xH2O (1.0 g, 3.0 mmol), ampdH2 (0.63 g, 6.0 mmol) and MeOH (7 ml) were combined in a Teflon-lined autoclave, heated at 393 K for 48 h, then cooled at 2 K h−1 to a very dark blue solution. Layering with Et2O gave violet cuboidal crystals (yield 30–35%), washed with MeOH and Et2O and dried under vacuum at 25 °C. Method 2: Cu(OAc)2·4H2O (0.24 g, 1.2 mmol), Ln(OAc)3·xH2O (0.4 g, 1.2 mmol) and ampdH2 (0.25 g, 2.4 mmol) in MeCN (50 ml) were stirred overnight, giving a light blue precipitate that was recrystallised by layering a concentrated MeOH solution with Et2O (yield <10%).",
